      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Amazon Bedrock AgentCore runtime gives these agents a fully managed, serverless environment: each session runs in its own isolated microVM, the platform scales to zero when there’s no work, and you only pay for the resources your sessions consume.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/architecture-patterns-for-fast-session-startup-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-runtime/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T22:02:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T02:20:36.971Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "AgentCore runtime with platformVersion set to “V2” changes how sessions start.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/architecture-patterns-for-fast-session-startup-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-runtime/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T22:02:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T02:20:36.971Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "This post explains how V2 starts a session, how to measure session start time, and how to keep work off the first request, including build hooks, which AgentCore runtime now supports.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/architecture-patterns-for-fast-session-startup-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-runtime/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T22:02:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T02:20:36.971Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "On V1, AgentCore pulls your container image from Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR), starts the container, and runs your initialization code before it can process the first request.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/architecture-patterns-for-fast-session-startup-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-runtime/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T22:02:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T02:20:36.971Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "When you create or update a runtime, AgentCore runtime starts your container in a fresh microVM and waits for the first healthy ping ( GET /ping ), which must arrive within 120 seconds.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/architecture-patterns-for-fast-session-startup-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-runtime/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T22:02:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T02:20:36.971Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Mount Amazon S3 Files or Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) during init, through an access point (requires virtual private cloud (VPC) mode)",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/architecture-patterns-for-fast-session-startup-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-runtime/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T22:02:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T02:20:36.971Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Leave them on the image, or move them to Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), S3 Files, or Amazon EFS",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/architecture-patterns-for-fast-session-startup-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-runtime/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T22:02:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T02:20:36.971Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Tool catalogs from AgentCore Gateway (a capability of Amazon Bedrock AgentCore), feature flags, and price lists change after you deploy.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/architecture-patterns-for-fast-session-startup-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-runtime/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T22:02:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T02:20:36.971Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "On V2, AgentCore runtime moves most of the work of starting a session to deployment time.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/architecture-patterns-for-fast-session-startup-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-runtime/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-13T22:02:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-14T02:20:36.971Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "To get started, set platformVersion to V2 when you create or update a runtime, then review Optimize your agent for AgentCore runtime V2 .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/architecture-patterns-for-fast-session-startup-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-runtime/",
